## Guardrails (summary — full list in `references/guardrails.md`)

- Tests define done. Never delete, skip or weaken a test; never disable a hook or CI check.
- Small diffs, one concern per branch. Stay inside the stack; new tech → `architect` agent → owner's OK.
- No secrets in code or logs. No destructive commands without the owner's OK.
- **Privacy:** {% if s.sensitive_data in ["Yes", "Not sure"] %}treat stored data as sensitive — least-privilege access, no
  personal data in logs, and flag data-protection rules that may apply.{% else %}normal data; users only ever see their own or shared data they're allowed to see.{% endif %}
{% if s.uses_ai == "Yes" %}- **AI features:** use {{ s.ai_provider }} from the server only; per-user usage limit; provider spending cap.
